A. the predicate against the positive control (every leg passed, met=True):
   leg=bind      leg_failed=True
   leg=sealed    leg_failed=True
   leg=code      leg_failed=True
   leg=twopass   leg_failed=True
   leg=envnames  leg_failed=True
   leg=hostlibs  leg_failed=False
   leg=rehash    leg_failed=True
   leg=newrow    leg_failed=False

B. a receipt relabelled to a leg that passed: verdict the harness would print
   m-member-flip labelled leg='code': met=False leg_failed=True -> ok
   m-text-flip labelled leg='rehash': met=False leg_failed=True -> ok
   m-ldpreload labelled leg='hostlibs': met=False leg_failed=False -> BATTERY-FAIL

   For comparison, the header field the harness never reads:
   m-member-flip: bind=1 sealed=1 code=1 teardown=1 newrow=1 bound=3/3 sealedruns=3/3 coderuns=3/3 envnames=3/3 hostlibs=3/3 anon=0 twopass=3/3 rehash=3 met=False
   m-text-flip: bind=0 sealed=1 code=0 teardown=1 newrow=1 bound=0/3 sealedruns=3/3 coderuns=0/3 envnames=3/3 hostlibs=3/3 anon=0 twopass=3/3 rehash=3 met=False
   m-ldpreload: bind=1 sealed=1 code=1 teardown=1 newrow=1 bound=3/3 sealedruns=3/3 coderuns=3/3 envnames=0/3 hostlibs=3/3 anon=0 twopass=3/3 rehash=0 met=False
